# Old Squarespace URLs -> new pages. 301 = permanent, which passes existing
# search ranking through to the new address.
#
# DO NOT add rules like "/services -> /services.html" here.
# Cloudflare Pages serves clean URLs natively: it already answers /services
# with services.html, and it 308-redirects /services.html -> /services. A rule
# pointing /services back at /services.html creates an infinite redirect loop,
# which is exactly what broke every nav link on the first deploy.
#
# Only list paths whose destination is a DIFFERENT page.

/appointments          /#book                     301
/appointments/         /#book                     301
/book                  /#book                     301
/booking               /#book                     301
/schedule              /#book                     301
/cart                  /                          301
/home                  /                          301
/store                 /                          301
/insurance             /faq#insurance             301
/insurance/            /faq#insurance             301
/journal               /blog                      301
/our-team              /team                      301
/emdr                  /trauma-emdr               301
/trauma                /trauma-emdr               301
/groups                /mamas-golden-hour         301
/group-therapy         /mamas-golden-hour         301
/mamas-golden-hour-group  /mamas-golden-hour      301

# No catch-all. Cloudflare Pages serves 404.html for unmatched paths on its
# own; a "/* -> /404.html" rule here intercepts real pages before they resolve.

# www/non-www: canonical tag says www, but nothing enforces it server-side,
# so both versions serve live and Google treats non-www as a duplicate.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE ON www REDIRECTS — do not re-add a rule like:
#     https://www.example.com/*  https://example.com/:splat  301!
#
# It does not work. Cloudflare Pages only matches _redirects sources as PATHS.
# An absolute URL in the source position is silently ignored, so the rule looks
# correct, deploys without error, and never fires. Verified empirically: the
# rule was added here and to two sibling sites, all three deployed, none
# redirected. Sites that DO canonicalize correctly (coolbirdcounseling.com,
# safersoundsclub.com) have no such rule in _redirects at all — theirs is done
# at the Cloudflare zone level.
#
# The fix lives in the Cloudflare dashboard, not this file:
#   Zone -> Rules -> Redirect Rules -> Create rule
#     If  Hostname equals <the hostname to retire>
#     Then Dynamic redirect, 301, preserving path and query
#
# Alternative if it must live in the repo: a Pages Function at
# functions/_middleware.js can redirect on hostname. That turns on the Functions
# runtime for every request on this project, so the dashboard rule is preferable
# for a purely static site.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
